    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190-a1">

                <pb facs="0614" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg492"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 239.
                    Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Margron to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Council of Secretaries of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 20,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: On account of the relations of
                    friendship that exist between the Republic of the United States and the Republic
                    of Hayti, the Government decides to make to the admiral the remise of the
                    merchant steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Haytien Republic</hi>, which was <pb
                        facs="0615" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> captured in the waters of St. Marc.
                    Nevertheless, the Government makes its reserves in what concerns the judiciary
                    action to which it can have recourse before the American courts.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eug. Margron</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Relations.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
